From: ossia <contact@ossia.io>
Subject: [PATCH] linuxcheck: skip when X11 is not found

target_include_directories() with an unset X11_X11_INCLUDE_PATH expands to
NOTFOUND and fails generation for the whole project, so score cannot be
configured on a distro built without x11.

Fixed upstream in ossia/score#2170; this is the minimal equivalent for 3.8.2.

Upstream-Status: Backport

--- a/src/linuxcheck/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/linuxcheck/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1,3 +1,7 @@
+if(NOT X11_FOUND)
+  return()
+endif()
+
 add_executable(linuxcheck
   x11.cpp
   wayland.cpp
